From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:44:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): stale-triage sweep releases a card once per
 triage entry, capped 3/day with a supervisor card [daveey]

sweep_stale_triage fired once per card ever (NOT EXISTS triage_swept). A card no chat
owns has no other releaser, so the second time it landed in triage (e.g. a drain kill
exhausting its failure budget again) it stayed there.

Now a card is eligible when a triage entry event (gave_up, block_loop_detected,
agent_block_escalated, supervisor_escalated, continuation_exhausted, blocked, status) is
newer than its last triage_swept. At most 3 sweeps per card in 24 h; past that the card
stays in triage with a triage_sweep_capped event and one board-supervisor card
(kanban.orchestrator_profile or default, created_by triage-sweep, idempotency key per
card per day) naming the card and its last 3 triage reasons, so it still has a producer.
The sweep moves to hermes_cli/kanban_triage_sweep.py; kanban_db_dispatch keeps the entry.
